 "summary": "Isangi territory (Tshopo), west of Kisangani along the Congo river at the Lomami and Aruwimi confluences, lies far from the eastern Kivu/Ituri conflict zones and no armed group is known to hold or administer any part of it as of the reference date. The state administers Isangi town (territorial seat) and Yangambi (INERA research centre and biosphere reserve), where the Congolese National Police (PNC) is the main day-to-day security force with a small FARDC presence. Rural villages of the Isangi, Yabaondo, Yakusu and Yahisuli secteurs are assessed under default state presence; local land, chieftaincy and boundary disputes and occasional banditry or poaching on the river are not known to have produced lasting non-state control. Web research could not be performed for this unit (search budget exhausted, news sites egress-blocked), so confidence is medium for the towns and low elsewhere.",
